course: dictionary
lesson: 3234
title: Entrust: giving something to look after
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To entrust something to someone means you hand it over for them to look after, because you trust them to keep it safe. «She entrusted me with her keys.» The key idea is trust: she believed I would take good care of them.
explain: You can entrust a thing or a person. In a story, a king might entrust a secret message to a brave messenger. At school, a teacher might entrust the class pet to a pupil for the holidays.
explain: Look at the patterns. You can entrust somebody with something, as in «entrusted me with her keys», or entrust something to somebody. Both mean the same. To check a meaning, swap in "gave to look after" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Church words use the same idea in a deeper way. «The Church of England uses funeral words... to «commend» someone to God means to entrust them to God's care.» Christians put themselves, or the dead, into God's care.
fact: Entrust means to give someone a job, a thing or a person to look after, because you trust them.
fact: «She entrusted me with her keys.» means she gave me her keys to look after because she trusted me.
fact: Entrust is a verb, so it changes: entrust, entrusts, entrusted, entrusting.
fact: In church, to entrust someone to God means to put them into God's care, as in funeral words.
fact: You can say entrust somebody with something, or entrust something to somebody.
exercise: «The teacher entrusted Mia with the class pet for the holidays.» What does entrusted mean here? | Forgot about the pet completely | Bought a new pet for Mia | Chased Mia away from the pet | *Gave Mia the job of looking after the pet, because she trusted her
exercise: Ben reads, «we entrust our sister to God's mercy» in a funeral. What does entrust mean in this phrase? | To steal someone away from God | To feel very cold | *To put someone into God's care | To tell God a secret joke
exercise: Which word is the past tense of entrust? | entrusting | *entrusted | entrusts | entrust
test: Mum will ___ the baby to you while she shops. Which word fits best? | entrusted | *entrust | entrusting | entrusts
test: Which word means about the same as entrust, when a teacher gives you the class pet to care for? | Forget | *Put in charge of | Argue about | Throw away
exam: The head teacher entrusted Ana with the school keys. What does entrusted mean? | Copied the keys for everyone | Took the keys away from Ana | Lost the keys in the playground | *Gave Ana the keys to look after, because she trusted her
